#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:13
#: 8c014b1d181e4e9291d41c5b3d805d13
msgid "1. Architectural Motivation & Subsystem Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:15
#: 22b0949da312473c89f3579a02cc6f29
msgid ""
"Directory traversal, hierarchical `.gitignore` evaluation, shebang "
"extraction, and magic-byte header inspection execute once per candidate "
"filesystem entry. On large monorepos containing tens of thousands of "
"files, Python object allocation and per-file I/O overhead dominate total "
"wall-clock execution time. At the same time, `findfmt`'s command-line "
"interface (`Typer` and `Rich`), 14 structured and visual output "
"serializers, layered TOML/environment configuration, and GNU `gettext` "
"localization benefit directly from Python's library ecosystem and PEP 561"
" static typing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:22
#: 9225cc36d12a43cda415efc0b2df5604
msgid ""
"To combine native I/O throughput with zero-regression portability, "
"`findfmt` separates native acceleration, runtime dispatch, and pure-"
"Python fallback across four explicit layers:"
