msgid "5. Native Engine Capabilities, Parity & Fuzzing Verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:126
#: a4a141d559944212bce30f27ce2e41fa
msgid ""
"Milestone `v1.4.1` delivers the complete native execution pipeline in "
"`findfmt_rs` (`#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:128
#: 71fe7778077c419fb8db707cbcbc8ea2
msgid ""
"**Streaming Directory Walker (`find_files_rs` / `find_files`)**: Executes"
" recursive traversal in Rust while releasing the Python `GIL` "
"(`py.detach`). Supports hierarchical `.gitignore`, `.git/info/exclude` "
"(including submodules and linked worktree `commondir` pointers), global "
"ignore files, `--gitignore-file`, linear-time PEP 383 `surrogateescape` "
"glob evaluation (`-P`, `-I`, `--ignore-case`, `--match-dirs`), depth and "
"entry boundaries (`-L`, `--filelimit`), single-filesystem confinement "
"(`-x`), symlink cycle detection (`-l`), resumable `--prune` discovery, "
"`--du` disk-usage accumulation, and deterministic natural version "
"sorting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:134
#: abdd657902e04e2c823dc61ce4e06b67
msgid ""
"**File Classification (`classify_file_rs` / `classify_file` / "
"`classify_batch_rs`)**: Opens regular files in `O_NONBLOCK` mode with "
"`fstat` regular-file verification to prevent hangs on swapped `FIFO` "
"pipes, extracts `#!` shebang tokens (including `env -S` and multiline "
"`nix-shell -i` headers), sniffs text vs. binary magic bytes, and resolves"
" `identify` format and `MIME` tags without holding the `GIL`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:138
#: 9b3e07621f4d460599152395940ac33d
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Parity, Property Testing & Continuous Fuzzing**: `tests/test_parity.py`"
" asserts 100% field-by-field `FileInfo` identity between "
"`findfmt._rust_ext` and `src/findfmt/_fallback.py`. Property-based "
"`proptest` suites (`findfmt_rs/tests/`), `cargo-fuzz` targets "
"(`findfmt_rs/fuzz/`), and `ClusterFuzzLite` harnesses (`tests/fuzz/`) "
"continuously stress-test arbitrary path bytes, malformed globs, shebang "
"headers, and binary buffers against panics and memory leaks."
msgstr ""
